.TH ENV 1.SH NAMEenv \- run a command in a changed environment.SH SYNOPSIS\fBenv\fR[\-i] [\-u name] [name=value ...] [command [argument ...]].SH DESCRIPTION\fBenv\fRis GNU env, from sh-utils 1.10.  It runs\fIcommand\fRwith each\fIname=value\fRadded to the environment it inherits:\fBenv FOO=bar printenv FOO\fRprints\fBFOO=bar\fR.\fRWith no command it prints the environment it would have used..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-i\fRstart from an empty environment; a lone\fB\-\fRmeans the same.  Long form\fB\-\-ignore\-environment\fR.\fR.TP 12\fB\-u\fI name\fRremove\fIname\fRfrom the environment.  Long form\fB\-\-unset=\fIname\fR.\fR.TP 12\fB\-\-help, \-\-version\fRwhat they say..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOprintenv, getenv